Git Fetch:- don't bring the actual files just the .git file from remote repo(github repo) to local repo(Desktop/shared folder)
Using git fetch will download the changes from github remote repo,
however you will not see those changes be part of the files you have
in the working directory.

Fetch allows you to grab additional work done on the remote master/main
branch, without needing to merge it in your working directory.
---Syntax---
git fetch <remote> <branch>
Example: git fetch origin <branch_name>
------------
Using git pull directly grabs the change as git fetch and merge the changes directly.
